Unless you consider the spoilers "game imbalance", it's basically just a
willingness to stop taking silly risks like fountain quaffing, and to
instead start using the tools the game provides you (Elbereth).

Whether some of the tools themselves are imbalanced is another story, and 
there is a reason that SporkHack exists, of course.  But it is nothing that
anyone needs to "get lucky" in order to use; it's just a question of
knowledge and willingness to use that same, along with recognition that
roguelikes are not real-time games and do not have to be played as
though they were.

